{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielraffel/Shipyard/pulls/784","id":4826230097,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR9hrG88AAAABH6ptUQ","html_url":"https://github.com/danielraffel/Shipyard/pull/784","diff_url":"https://github.com/danielraffel/Shipyard/pull/784.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/danielraffel/Shipyard/pull/784.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielraffel/Shipyard/issues/784","number":784,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: success-rate scorecard in metrics gate-cost","user":{"login":"shipyard-local[bot]","id":288178668,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOES1B7A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/shipyard-local","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\n`shipyard metrics gate-cost --scorecard` is the success-rate scorecard from the pre-push fast-failure audit (pulp-planning `2026-10-11-prepush-fast-failure-audit.md`, section 8 and Appendix C). The ruling promoted the scorecard to P1 so that P0-1, P0-2 and the toolchain bundle can each be shown to have moved a number.\n\nIt extends the existing `metrics gate-cost` surface rather than adding a tool. It reuses the gate-cost run listing, job reads, ejection-cause rule, cross-check and read cache. For each ISO week of `--from`/`--to` (or `--since`), per repository, it reports:\n\n- **open to merge**: median and p90 hours from `createdAt` to `mergedAt`, for pull requests merged into the base;\n- **merge-queue ejection rate**: merge-group runs whose final gate attempt did not pass, over runs whose final gate attempt completed. It reports `gate_failed` separately, and counts a run that failed while its gate passed apart from ejections;\n- **red-after-push rate**: among merged pull requests' commits that carry a required context, the share with a red required context. The latest run of each check name decides; `cancelled` is not red and is counted apart;\n- **repeat-failure classes**: check names red on two or more different merged pull requests, flagged when required.\n\nEverything is read from GitHub, so a past window can be measured again.\n\n## The traps it carries, each found in real data\n- A merge-group run concluding `failure` with its gate green is not an ejection (pulp 2026-W40: 274 such runs against 48 real gate failures).\n- A commit's checks past the first 100 are read. Pulp heads carry up to 103, and `Vellum trusted freeze` was on the second page.\n- Pull requests are listed by number, and each one's commits are read 25 to a page. Pages of whole pull requests with their checks answered HTTP 504 on a day with an 85-commit pull request, even on retry.\n- GitHub lists at most 250 commits of a pull request (#9755 answered 250 of 300). That is counted and named (`capped_prs`), not refused.\n- A gateway error (502/503/504) is retried up to 3 times. Any other error, or a lasting one, fails with only the tail of `gh`'s output, which otherwise prints every page it had read.\n- Every listing is checked against GitHub's own count, and a missing collection key is an error, never an empty list.\n- Required contexts come from classic branch protection, or `--required-context`. A ruleset that requires checks is refused rather than ignored. A required context that no merged commit carries is reported as a gap, because a misspelled one would otherwise read as a lower red rate.\n\n## Tests\nTwelve scorecard tests run against answers captured from `Generous-Corp/pulp` with the same queries the code sends (`tests/fixtures/gate-cost-scorecard/`). Their expected numbers were derived independently in Python from the same captures.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nAdds a success-rate scorecard to `shipyard metrics gate-cost` via a new `--scorecard` flag, reporting per ISO week: open-to-merge median and p90, merge-queue ejection rate, red-after-push rate on required checks, and check names red across two or more merged PRs. All numbers are read live from GitHub, so any past window covered by `--from`/`--to` can be re-measured.\n\n- Ejection rate now counts GitHub's own queue removals (`failed_checks`/`checks_timed_out` by `github-merge-queue` over queue entries), not failed gate runs; gate failures are reported separately.\n- Required contexts come from branch protection or `--required-context`; a required context absent from all merged commits is reported as a gap.\n- Handles GitHub's limits: checks past 100 are paged, a PR's commits are read 25 per page, and a PR with more than 250 commits is counted as `capped_prs` rather than partially read.\n- Gateway errors (502/503/504) are retried up to 3 times; other errors fail with only the tail of `gh` output.\n- Includes tests against captured `Generous-Corp/pulp` answers, with expected numbers derived independently in Python, including a pinned 2026-W41 verdict of 38 ejections.\n\n<sup>Written for commit fd0e94e25f447578256f3aae97cc0ab6103d5f0c. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/danielraffel/Shipyard/pull/784?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://www.cubic.dev/action/auto-fix/pr/danielraffel/Shipyard/784?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdanielraffel%2FShipyard%2Fpull%2F784&source=description\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Turn on auto-fix\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/turn-on-auto-fix-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n<!-- whence {\"labels\": [\"1·claude\", \"2·m3\", \"5·subrouter\"], \"prov\": {\"agent\": \"claude\", \"host\": \"m3\", \"launcher\": \"cmux\", \"terminal\": \"cmux\", \"terminal_address\": \"00FD407D-DAED-4046-992F-8E0EF9BA146C\", \"route\": \"subrouter\", \"origin_state\": \"lookup_failed\", \"path\": \"/Volumes/Workshop/Code/agent-worktrees/sy-impl3-scorecard\", \"session\": \"08fb81d8-38a3-4b20-8bcc-c34ba2a66ffb\", \"config_home\": \"~/.subrouter/codex/claude-proxy/25bf8e1a2393f1108d37029b\", \"resume\": \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=\\\"$HOME/.subrouter/codex/claude-proxy/25bf8e1a2393f1108d37029b\\\" claude \\u002d\\u002dresume 08fb81d8-38a3-4b20-8bcc-c34ba2a66ffb\", \"jump\": \"cmux surface focus 00FD407D-DAED-4046-992F-8E0EF9BA146C\", \"relaunch\": \"cmux surface resume get \\u002d\\u002dsurface 00FD407D-DAED-4046-992F-8E0EF9BA146C\"}} -->\n\n---\n### 🔎 Provenance\n\n|  |  |\n|:--|:--|\